{
	title: 'Ctrl-G toggles the terminal gutter',
	spec: 'The client-only command /gutter, bound to Ctrl-G and listed in /keys under Clipboard, toggles the blank column at both sides of the transcript rows, so text and links copied from the transcript reach both edges, as Pi output padding does. The prompt, tab, status, help and notice rows keep their columns, so the prompt cursor stays on the screen; a plugin may change them. Toggling clears the cached row layouts and repaints in full. The setting lasts for the client run; the old Hal had the same key (tasks/cc/terminal.md).',
	status: 'done',
	needs: ['cc']
}
